id: pm-ye9v2t
title: "GH-826: extension commands need structured failure results and preserved remediation"
description: "Extension handlers cannot return a machine-readable report with a non-zero process status, while thrown handler remediation and codes are replaced by generic host guidance."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:sdk",error-contract,extensions,github-intake
created_at: "2026-07-30T11:28:13.431Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T17:04:19.474Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: CommandHandlerResult carries a validated non-zero exit channel; structured payloads still render on failure; extension error code and remediation survive host rendering; CLI and SDK integration tests cover both returned and thrown failures
goal: project management = context management
objective: Give extension gates the same structured verdict and recovery contract as core commands
value: "Custom lint, policy, changelog, and preflight commands can serve both CI and agents"
impact: Removes the forced choice between structured output and a truthful process exit code
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
